          "type": "response_end",
          "response": {
            "text": "Alberto's Fraud Detection Agent reviews newly published events and organizers on an online event ticketing platform. For each one, it recommends approve, reject, or request info, along with its reasons, and a human admin makes the final decision.\n\nIt uses graded autonomy: it auto-approves only on evidence verified in code, and web sources can hold a decision back but never approve it.\n\nThe agent is at the offline-evals stage. On 31 test cases, the Claude Haiku 5.5 model was chosen for deployment, with 86% accuracy and 1% of fraud approved, at about $0.002 per review. It is built with TypeScript, PostgreSQL and GCP.",
